 "notes": "Fol. 51v contains the colophon to an embedded or preceding work (Vaidyamanotsava by Nainasukha, son of Sodāsa), while fol. 93r concludes Kokamañjarī by Ānanda. The phrase 'thāsā phocoya sidhuko juro' is a Newari expression representing 'thva saphū coyā sidhuko julo' ('the copying of this book is completed'), not a place name. The catalogue reads the scribe's name as Dhuṃju, but the manuscript reads Dhaṃju.",
